ese are substantial theorem uses, not fixed calculations.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/inference/argument/2/text\",\"/logic/calculations/0\"]},\"dependency_accounting\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The prose uses substantive facts not accounted for by the listed H/M inputs: compact subsets of Euclidean space are bounded; dim_H of bounded subsets of R^n is at most n; the stated Hausdorff-content/measure relationships; dimension monotonicity under Lipschitz maps; and dim_H([0,1])=1. The author-written calculation policy covers product-distance and diameter inequalities only and cannot import those results. M001/M002 do not establish these missing facts.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/inference/argument/2/text\",\"/logic/calculations/0\",\"/inference/inputs\"]},\"output\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The declared output is the target statement dim_H(E×I)=dim_H(E)+1. S001–S003 purport to establish upper and lower bounds and combine them into equality, so the intended conclusion matches the output; the failure is validity, not a different stated target.\",\"locations\":[\"/output/statement\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/inference/argument/2/text\"]},\"scope\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The proof divides according to D>0 and D=0, but does not establish that D is a finite nonnegative real or that these cases exhaust its possible Hausdorff-dimension value in the packet's stated critical-exponent convention. In particular S001's unproved D≤n is needed to justify the finite-exponent reasoning and choosing q>D. The locally fixed q, δ, s, ε and cover choices are not discharged through explicit quantified statements; the prose merely says to take limits/infima and combine bounds.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/locals/0\",\"/inference/locals/2\",\"/inference/locals/3\",\"/inference/locals/5\",\"/inference/locals/6\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/inference/argument/2/text\"]},\"applicability\":{\"verdict\":\"UNVERIFIED\",\"notes\":\"The packet supplies intended bindings for both M inputs, but does not provide full ambient constructions/proofs for the applications. M001 is intended for E in Euclidean Borel space and a positive exponent below D; the bridge from the prose's real s to the NNReal exponent and the exact metric/Borel setup are only asserted. M002's countable index and indicator measurability are described, but the restricted-measure integral identity and its identification with the required cover sum are not fully established. These application concerns are additional to the earlier unsupported implication.\",\"locations\":[\"/inputs/2/source_contract\",\"/inputs/3/source_contract\",\"/inference/applications/0\",\"/inference/applications/1\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\"]},\"statement_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The output formula is explicit, but the local Hausdorff content symbol is only described as an infimum of Nat-indexed δ-cover sums; the covered set, precise admissible-cover conditions, scale convention, and exponentiation conventions are not completely stated. S002 also relies on unstated content/measure relationships. The packet does not give a fully specified local meaning adequate to check those formulas from the packet alone.\",\"locations\":[\"/output/statement\",\"/inference/locals/13/declaration\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\"]},\"object_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The prose introduces covers of E and F, countable indexing, projections, intervals enclosing projected sets, and Hausdorff contents/measure scales. Some are named as locals, but their types/declarations do not establish existence or the stated properties. In particular r_j is declared as a witness from compactness without an input/local existence proof that supplies arbitrarily small q-cost covers, and chosen intervals J_i are declared while the text needs their existence and width properties. x₀, by contrast, is legitimately witnessed from H001.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/locals/4\",\"/inference/locals/7\",\"/inference/locals/8\",\"/inference/locals/9\",\"/inference/locals/10\",\"/inference/locals/11\",\"/inference/locals/12\",\"/inference/locals/13\",\"/inference/locals/14\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/inference/argument/2/text\"]},\"dependency_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"Reverse-reading factual uses reveals unlisted/unproved theorem content, beginning in S001 with compactness implying boundedness and dim_H(E)≤n. Later S002/S003 uses content-limit equivalences, Hausdorff dimension monotonicity under Lipschitz maps, and the interval's dimension. None is a direct input or fully derived local fact. M001 and M002 cannot supply these unrelated statements.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/inference/argument/2/text\",\"/inference/inputs\",\"/inputs/2\",\"/inputs/3\"]},\"packet_replay\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Sufficiency judgment is based only on the full packet.json and declared Yui Audit A/self-containment/format rules read for this task. Packet alone contains enough prose and input declarations to identify the first unsupported implication and reject the inference; no outside source proof or other mathematical task material was needed. This is a statement about packet-only mathematical sufficiency, not runtime/carrier authentication or canonical hash binding.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inputs/1/statement\",\"/parameters\",\"/logic/calculations/0\",\"/warning\"]}},\"findings\":[{\"location\":\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"severity\":\"blocking\",\"finding\":\"First unsupported implication: H002 (E compact) ⇒ E bounded, followed by the assertion that bounded Euclidean box cube coverings imply dim_H(E)≤n. Neither implication is proved in this packet or supplied as an input. Therefore the first upper-bound step does not close.\"},{\"location\":\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"severity\":\"blocking\",\"finding\":\"The content lower-bound argument imports several unproved substantive links between infinite Hausdorff measure, scale contents, cover comparisons, and Hausdorff dimension. M001 and M002 do not prove those links.\"},{\"location\":\"/inference/argument/2/text\",\"severity\":\"blocking\",\"finding\":\"Projection monotonicity for Hausdorff dimension and dim_H(I)=1 are used without a direct input or local proof. The n=0 discussion also does not prove its asserted isometry/dimension conclusion.\"}]}}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read an explicitly frozen task document by ID; no other local files are accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["id","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_yui","description":"Read declared Yui rules/templates; no tests, historical runs or personal files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_artifact","description":"Check a JSON artifact against the explicit stage contract; this is not automatic mathematical certification.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_artifact","description":"Submit a JSON artifact after its stage checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json